  "The parts are the same as in step 1. I added nothing and dropped nothing.",
  "I built the potentiometer version. The photoresistor version is an alternative and is not built.",
  "The potentiometer sits in one breadboard row (10t.a, 11t.a, 12t.a) in the order GND, SIG, VCC. Each wire goes into the same column as its potentiometer pin: GND to Uno GND, SIG to A0 and VCC to 5V. The image shows red for 5V, black for GND and yellow for A0.",
  "The optional external LED circuit follows the page text. Pin 13 goes through wire4 to the 220 ohm resistor, then to the LED anode. The LED cathode goes by wire5 to the GND pin next to pin 13. The text image for this circuit did not load.",
  "The catalogue has three GND ports on the Uno (GND.1, GND.2, GND.3). I assumed GND.3 is the header pin next to pin 13, and used GND.1 for the potentiometer."
